 "guide": [
  "Addresses are eboot RVAs for PPSA01341 01.007.000. Guest RIP is 0x900000000 plus the RVA. Code file offset = RVA + 0xFE50. One cheat page, 0x8004000 through 0x8008000. off and on are the same length. The big page at 8004000 is 5496 bytes and ends at 0x8005578. The archstone gate at 8005600 sits after it, still inside the page.",
  "The world and the UI are different pictures. 90ae7f stores 3440/1440 into the display object at [rbx+4], which is the gameplay aspect. That is why the hall fills 3440x1440 without stretch. The data sites and the mov-immediate sites retarget 2560x1440 and 3840x2160 entries to 3440x1440 and 5160x2160. Those immediates were tested: forcing them does not slide the UI. Leave them. Do not shrink the shared scanout or backbuffer.",
  "The HUD hook is e244a5 into 8004000. When the box is taller than 800 and its aspect is between 1.40 and 2.60, width becomes height times 16/9 (bytes 39 8e e3 3f at cave offset 0x55) and the slack is split to both X edges. A second check then adds 330 to both edges when the height is over 1000 and the width is over 1600. 330 in this 1920x1080 UI space is the 440-pixel screen margin. This is why health, the diamonds, and the menus that use that canvas are centered. The hook only ever sees that full canvas (left 330, right 2250, height 1080 after the shift). A 1920-wide box already passes the 1600 test. The darkened offering plate does not come through here, so changing 1600 does not center it.",
  "The offering dim, the logos, and the cinematics are 16:9 content in a 5160x2160 UI texture that is presented from x=0. 912465 jumps to 8004100, which publishes that texture at origin 0,0 with its full size, then continues at 912481 into 911e70. 911ef4 is nopped so the upload uses the texture's own size. Shifting that origin by 660 centered the dim and also moved the HUD and the menus, because they are drawn into the same texture. Taking the HUD's 330 away at the same time put the HUD on the left edge. Neither of those experiments is in this file. Do not add 660 to every 5160-wide viewport: the hall is 5160 wide too, and it slides off the screen. The UI renderer global is 0x2F0A988. Do not use 0x2F0ACF8.",
  "911f23 jumps to 8004180. That cave writes [rbp-8] = [rbp-0x28] + 0x1dc and returns to 911f28. The write is the picture pointer. Nopping it removes the Nexus world, the player, and the NPCs. An add of 660 to [rbp-0x94] is still assembled later in the page and is skipped. Putting that add back slices the frame into vertical strips.",
  "Archstone captions are a different store. dd61f4 jumps to 8005600. X is increased by 660 only when Y is within 2 of 660 or 1408, in the 5160x2160 target. The add at 8005647 jumps to 8005A00, which skips the 660 when X is within 2 of 1051 or 1219. Those two values are the arrow counts. Every other caption, including the archstone words, still gets 660. Do not nop the add and do not widen the window of 2. The gate saves ymm1 and ymm2 because clobbering them blanks the inventory item mesh.",
  "The hooks at 90e7a8, 90df87, 90e0ad, 90e205, 90ebb9, 911e70, dd5d4c, dd84b4, and 91452c are leftover probes in the same page. They log, and the code that would edit the picture is behind a flag dword that is 0. Leave the flags at 0. Do not slide the four item quads: both X corners have to move together or the quad shears, and while the HUD is 16:9 the vertices are submitted and then discarded. Do not hook 9124d3 or copy picture slot 0 into slot 4; that turns the frame green. 90ebb9 does not run during normal play.",
  "The position getter epilogue at e0afe3 jumps to 8005700. That cave adds 330 unless some parent is already at 330. It also leaves button labels alone when the widget stores its own final position and X is past 400, leaves the keystone wording alone, leaves an area-name column alone, leaves the leave-game confirm row alone. A node at local X 159.5 and Y 240 is the leave-game divider. The exit at 8005e00 pulls that group back by 61, pulls the 2-tall rule another 40, and gives those 40 back to the name row so Der Nexus lines up with the class and the time. A 400 by 300 column at local Y 120 comes back by 21, and the 629 by 20 header at local Y 40 comes back by 21, so the block sits in the card. The confirm row and its gold button each gain 19. A selection bar between 395 and 445 wide and 76 to 84 tall loses 330 when one of the next three parents is already at its final X, so the glow stays on the label. e0a2bb jumps to 8005c00, which sets the card extra to 141.6 and the confirm wrap extra to 971.6 and adds 80 to that rule. Those together uncover the gold point and make the rule meet both stat lines. Shrine frames, eyes, and the decorative rules do get the 330. The twin reader epilogue at e0ae97 jumps to the same 8005700 cave, so the leave-game stat clip moves with the text. That shows Seelenstufe, the soul level, the class, and the play time. Do not hook e0b300. Still open: the inventory item preview, which is centered in an 860x360 picture while its frame is narrower, and the boot logos through the first spawn. Do not ship a logger in this file."
 ],
